# bp-confusion heatmap (local-mode View A)

**What this is.** Pooled across every selected sample × haplotype
× (cluster, chrom): a confusion matrix between the FLARE
per-site label and the popout per-site label, where each cell is
weighted by the segment length in bp. Rows are FLARE labels;
columns are popout labels; cells are row-normalised so each row
sums to 1 of bp share.

**How to read this chart.** Diagonal mass = agreement at the
nucleotide level. Strong off-diagonal mass on a specific row
means popout systematically calls those bp under a different
label than FLARE. The title strip shows the overall diagonal
fraction.

